course: dictionary
lesson: 2047
title: Connect: joining things and ideas
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Connect means to join two or more things together so they touch or are linked. «Connect the wires» means join the wires so that electricity can flow between them.
explain: The same word works for ideas too. «Connect the clues» means see how the clues are related, so they fit together and help you find the answer.
explain: Connect can also mean feel close to someone and understand them. «She really connects with children» means she is good at making children feel understood.
explain: Check the meaning in the sentence. Ask yourself: is something being joined, linked or understood here? If your meaning fits, you are probably right.
fact: Connect is a verb: connect, connects, connected, connecting.
fact: «Everything is connected» means every part of the world is linked to every other part.
fact: In maths, you connect dots, points and lines to draw shapes.
fact: Useful phrases: «connect to», «connect with», «stay connected».
fact: Safety: never connect things to the mains yourself, and never connect the two ends of a battery directly.
exercise: In science you «connect the wires» to a battery to make a circuit. What does connect mean here? | Cut the wires into small pieces | Paint the wires a bright colour | Hide the wires under the desk | *Join the wires so they touch and make a circuit
exercise: «She really connects with children.» What does connects with mean? | Counts them quickly | Walks past them | Shouts at them | *Feels close to them and understands them
exercise: The train will connect with the bus, so you can change from one to the other. What does connect mean here? | *Meet another so you can change from one to the other | Stop moving for a while | Hit something hard | Lose your ticket
test: «Connect the clues» means: | Write each clue twice | Throw the clues away | Count the clues quickly | *Work out how the clues are related
test: Linking words such as «however» and «because» show how ideas ___. | Shrink | Bounce | *Connect | Freeze
exam: Pupil says, «Everything is connected.» What does this suggest about the world? | Everything is the same colour | Nothing ever changes | *Every part of the world is linked to the others | Only phones are important
